### 🚁 What is the Helicopter Racing League?
The Helicopter Racing League is a global sports franchise where pilots compete in high-speed, low-altitude helicopter races. Because of the extreme nature of the sport, the league relies heavily on cutting-edge technology to ensure safety, analyze performance, and engage fans worldwide.
| Aspect | Description |
|---|---|
| **Core Product** | Live-streamed aerial races with telemetry data tracked in real-time. |
| **Media & Broadcast** | High-definition (HD) and operational video feeds from onboard cameras, trackside cameras, and drones. |
| **Fan Experience** | Real-time statistics, global video-on-demand (VOD), and interactive telemetry overlays for viewers. |
---
### ⚙️ The Cloud Architecture & Business Challenges
In its capacity as a Google Cloud architecture scenario, the HRL is used to design solutions for specific business and technical challenges:
*   **Real-Time Telemetry:** Over 100 sensors per helicopter transmit operational data (engine temperature, speed, rotor RPM, altitude) every fraction of a second. This requires a robust ingest pipeline like **Google Cloud Pub/Sub** and stream processing via **Dataflow**.
*   **Video Processing & Distribution:** Racing video must be ingested, transcoded, and served globally with low latency. This leverages **Cloud CDN**, **Cloud Storage**, and **Media CDN**.
*   **Predictive Analytics:** The league uses machine learning (ML) models built on **Vertex AI** to predict race outcomes, analyze pilot behavior, and monitor helicopter maintenance needs proactively to prevent mechanical failures.
*   **Global Scalability:** Because races happen in remote locations around the world, the infrastructure must be hybrid-ready and capable of handling sudden spikes in traffic during live events.
---
